{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-substrate-line-bundle","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:substrate-line-bundle","kind":"definition","title":"The substrate line bundle and the $\\mathbb{G}_m$-family of differentials","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-substrate-parameter"],"tags":["line-bundle","multiplicative-group","projective","substrate","family"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.FluidDynamics.SubstrateLineBundle","text":"substrate-line-bundle.md","leanSource":"substrate-line-bundle.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:substrate-line-bundle\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a <a href=\"#def:quantum-observable-universe\" data-at=\"quantum-observable-universes/qou-definition\">QOU</a> equipped with <a href=\"#def:weight-decomposition\" data-at=\"quantum-observable-universes/weight-decomposition\">weight decomposition</a> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\pi_H, \\pi_V)</code> and <a href=\"#def:categorical-reeb\" data-at=\"quantum-observable-universes/differential-structures-reeb\">Reeb derivation</a> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\xi</code>.</p>\n<p>The <strong>substrate line bundle</strong> is the trivial <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{G}_m</code>-torsor</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\mathcal{Q}\n  = \n  \\mathrm{End}(\\mathbf{1}) \\otimes_\\mathbb{Z} \\mathbb{G}_m\n   \\to \n  \\mathrm{Spec}R,</code></pre>\n<p>with fibre <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{G}_m(R) = R^\\times</code> over each <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-point. A <strong>substrate section</strong> is a global section <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\colon \\mathrm{Spec}R \\to \\mathcal{Q}</code>, that is, an element <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\in R^\\times</code>.</p>\n<p>Over <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{G}_m = \\mathrm{Spec}\\mathbb{Z}[q, q^{-1}]</code>, the <strong>universal substrate differential</strong> is</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\mathbf{d}\n  = \n  q^{-1}d + (1 - q^{-1})\\pi_V \\circ d\n   \\in \n  \\mathrm{Hom}_{\\mathbb{Z}[q,q^{-1}]}\\!\n  \\bigl(\\Omega^k(A), \\Omega^{k+1}(A)\\bigr).</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/substrate-line-bundle.md","heading":"Definition","number":"20.5.7","page":"b/def-substrate-line-bundle","qa":{"counts":{"pass":82,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":9,"unknown":0,"stale":66},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.FluidDynamics.SubstrateLineBundle","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/substrate-line-bundle.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
